# A config file that is not valid JSON is an error path: tchori validate exits
# non-zero, writes nothing to stdout, and reports one structured diagnostic per
# line on stderr (JSON, because stderr is a pipe and not a TTY). Config parsing
# fails before any provider is resolved, so this needs no provider binary and
# no network. The detail is asserted only as far as the offending file name;
# the text after it comes from encoding/json and is not tchori's contract.

! exec tchori validate
! stdout .
stderr '"severity":"error"'
stderr '"summary":"invalid JSON in config file"'
stderr '"detail":"main\.tchori\.json: '

-- main.tchori.json --
{ not json
